        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.645,
            0.064,
            0.834,
            0.081
          ],
          "content": "The Other Side of Zero"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.12,
            0.74,
            0.161
          ],
          "content": "Floor +3 is lower than Floor +4. So, we write +3 < +4. We also write +4 > +3."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.164,
            0.533,
            0.186
          ],
          "content": "Should we write –3 < – 4 or – 4 < – 3?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.191,
            0.74,
            0.232
          ],
          "content": "Floor – 4 is lower than Floor – 3. So, – 4 < – 3. It is also correct to write – 3 > – 4"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.242,
            0.301,
            0.264
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Figure it Out"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.158,
            0.272,
            0.741,
            0.315
          ],
          "content": "1. Compare the following numbers using the Building of Fun and fill in the boxes with < or >."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.197,
            0.322,
            0.329,
            0.346
          ],
          "content": "a. $-2 \\xrightarrow{ 一 } +5$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.197,
            0.348,
            0.331,
            0.371
          ],
          "content": "d. $+6 \\bigtriangleup -6$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.414,
            0.324,
            0.547,
            0.347
          ],
          "content": "b. – 5 +4"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.596,
            0.324,
            0.728,
            0.347
          ],
          "content": "c. – 5 – 3"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.415,
            0.349,
            0.535,
            0.373
          ],
          "content": "e. 0 –4"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.595,
            0.349,
            0.718,
            0.372
          ],
          "content": "f. 0 +4"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.208,
            0.393,
            0.739,
            0.469
          ],
          "content": "Notice that all negative number floors are below Floor 0. So, all negative numbers are less than 0. All the positive number floors are above Floor 0. So, all positive numbers are greater than 0."
